@format 1
@id media-preview.common.flyleaf-preview
@title Flyleaf preview
@section Media preview
@area Common
@entry flyleaf-start
@summary Trace Flyleaf eligibility, opening, viewer-state commit, synchronous media publication, and only then preview/autoplay restoration.
@related media-preview.common.media-publication
@tag media
@tag preview
@tag common
@tag flyleaf

@alias viewer = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PViewer

[flyleaf-start] Flyleaf preview path <input>
~ The preview uses the selected preview engine for this path.
[Technical explanation]
= The completion router or current mpv fallback selected Flyleaf for this source.
> eligibility

[eligibility] Flyleaf media eligibility <decision>
~ The program checks whether this media can be shown by the selected preview engine.
[Technical explanation]
- Reject audio-only media when the viewer does not permit audio-only sources @ viewer.PPlayerMediaApply(...)
? "Audio-only source disallowed" > restricted
? "Media allowed" > open

[restricted] Restricted-source commit request <process>
~ The program prepares to accept a media source that has limited preview support.
[Technical explanation]
- Prepare the PViewerMediaCommit call with no Flyleaf player and cargo containing the audio-only restriction @ viewer.PPlayerMediaApply(...)
> restricted-ready

[open] Flyleaf preview opening <external>
~ The preview engine starts opening the selected media.
[Technical explanation]
- Create or reuse a Flyleaf player, configure it, apply volume, open the source, pause it, and seek to the start @ viewer.PPlayerMediaApply(...)
  @ viewer.PPlayerFlyleafOpen(...)
  @ viewer.PPlayerStartPause(...)
> open-result

[restricted-ready] Restricted commit ready <junction>
> commit-join

[open-result] Flyleaf opening result <decision>
~ The program checks whether the preview engine opened the media successfully.
[Technical explanation]
- Recheck viewer lifetime/load ownership and dispose a newly created unattached player when the request became stale @ viewer.PPlayerMediaApply(...)
? "Viewer request became stale" > stale
? "Viewer request still current" > commit-join

[commit-join] Flyleaf commit inputs converge <junction>
> commit-state

[stale] Stale Flyleaf result ignored <output>
~ This path ends with stale preview engine result ignored.
[Technical explanation]
= An obsolete Flyleaf result does not replace current viewer state.

[commit-state] Commit viewer identity and preview host <process>
~ The preview makes this media file current and attaches the preview display.
[Technical explanation]
- In PViewerMediaCommit, record the outcome, swap or reuse the player, update preview visibility, assign media information and PViewerSourcePath, set stopped playback state, and reset nonpersistent crop state @ viewer.PViewerMediaRecord(...)
  @ viewer.PViewerMediaCommit(...)
> publish

[publish] Synchronous viewer-media publication <process>
~ The preview immediately announces that its current media changed.
[Technical explanation]
- Invoke PViewerMediaRaise before any autoplay, preview restoration, or final playback-state update; Media preview / Media publication details the subscriber call @ viewer.PViewerMediaRaise(...)
! PViewerMediaRaise returns to PViewerMediaCommit before the remaining preview/playback work continues.
> player-check

[player-check] Usable Flyleaf player present <decision>
~ The program checks usable preview engine player present.
[Technical explanation]
- Continue according to whether PViewerMediaCommit received a usable player @ viewer.PViewerMediaCommit(...)
? "No player" > no-player-stop
? "Player ready" > autoplay-check

[no-player-stop] No-preview playback state <process>
~ This step handles no-preview playback state.
[Technical explanation]
- Set playback to stopped at zero and return after publication @ viewer.PViewerPlaybackUpdate(...)
> no-player-wait

[autoplay-check] Autoplay preference <decision>
~ The program checks autoplay preference.
[Technical explanation]
- After publication, branch on the current autoplay preference @ viewer.PViewerMediaCommit(...)
? "Autoplay enabled" > autoplay
? "Autoplay disabled" > paused

[no-player-wait] No-preview completion alignment <junction>
> complete-join

[autoplay] Restore preview and start playback <process>
~ This step handles restore preview and start playback.
[Technical explanation]
- Play, restore preview state, publish playing/time state, and start the viewer clock @ viewer.PViewerMediaCommit(...)
  @ viewer.PViewerPreviewRestore(...)
  @ viewer.PViewerPlaybackUpdate(...)
> complete-join

[paused] Restore preview while stopped <process>
~ This step handles restore preview while stopped.
[Technical explanation]
- Restore preview state and publish stopped-at-zero playback state @ viewer.PViewerMediaCommit(...)
  @ viewer.PViewerPreviewRestore(...)
  @ viewer.PViewerPlaybackUpdate(...)
> complete-join

[complete-join] Flyleaf completion convergence <junction>
> flyleaf-complete

[flyleaf-complete] Flyleaf commit finished <output>
~ The preview has finished switching to the new media.
[Technical explanation]
= Viewer-media subscribers ran before the final preview/autoplay state was applied.
